on disjunction and exclusive disjunction as silent updates plus four reporting orderings that forward prior contents, together with a full ordering exchange that replaces contents and forwards prior contents."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_and","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_fetch_and","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_set","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_read","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_try_cmpxchg","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_xchg"],"text":"Each wrapper performs any checker and sanitizer annotation first and then delegates the state transition to the matching underlying primitive of the same operation and ordering, preserving silent versus reporting shape so the caller visible result is exactly the underlying outcome."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_fetch_and","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_read","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_set","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_try_cmpxchg","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_try_cmpxchg_release"],"text":"Update wrappers annotate the full extent of the referenced atomic object for both read and write, loads annotate for read only, stores annotate for write only, and holder compare wrappers additionally annotate the full extent of the caller old holder for both read and write, always ahead of delegation."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_fetch_and","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_sub_and_test","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_add_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_xchg","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_fetch_and_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_set_release","include/linux/atom